\paragraph{Permutation null distribution.}
To formally establish statistical significance, we run 1,000 permutations, randomly reassigning temporal labels while preserving group sizes.
Table~\ref{tab:permutation} summarizes the results: the null distribution has mean C\%\,=\,0.21\% ($\text{SD}$\,=\,0.05\%), consistent with the random-split control (0.18\%).
The observed 31.3\% lies $>$600$\sigma$ above the null mean ($p < 0.001$), providing overwhelming evidence that temporal DIF is real.

