\paragraph{Cross-benchmark portability: GSM8K.}
Table~\ref{tab:gsm8k} summarizes the three-step GSM8K validation.
The framework successfully transfers: temporal C\%\,=\,18.9\% (lower than MMLU, consistent with single-domain structure), semi-synthetic $\Delta$TPR\,=\,+0.818 (standard matching).
The GSM1K external validation yields $r$\,=\,$-$0.478 ($p$\,=\,0.005, $N$\,=\,33)---DIF flags \emph{anti-correlate} with contamination gaps.
This negative correlation, while based on a small sample and wide confidence intervals, suggests DIF on GSM8K captures capability-driven rather than contamination-driven item functioning changes.
We report this as exploratory evidence, not a core claim.

