\subsection{Downstream Impact: Instability $\neq$ Invalidity}
\label{sec:downstream}

\paragraph{Graceful degradation under item replacement.}
Table~\ref{tab:degradation} shows benchmark validity metrics under progressive replacement of DIF-flagged items.
Even at 31\% replacement (matching the observed C\%), ranking correlation remains $\rho$\,=\,0.990, reliability $\alpha$\,=\,0.935, and construct coverage 0.89.
At 50\% replacement, all metrics remain within acceptable ranges ($\rho$\,=\,0.978, $\alpha$\,=\,0.912).
The theoretical bound $\rho \geq 1 - 0.45r$ (where $r$ is the replacement fraction) fits the empirical data with correlation 0.994, indicating degradation is predictable and manageable.

