In contrast, traditional detectors degrade substantially on reasoning-RL models (Table~\ref{tab:rl-detectors}): Min-K\% AUROC drops from 0.72 to 0.48 ($\Delta$\,=\,$-$0.24, DeLong $p$\,=\,0.001), and ConStat from 0.68 to 0.51 ($\Delta$\,=\,$-$0.17, $p$\,=\,0.008).
DIF's group-level design is naturally immune to individual-model signal perturbation from RL training.

