\label{app:constat}

We independently evaluate ConStat-style perturbation testing on 250 LLM-paraphrased MMLU items across 50 models.
Table~\ref{tab:constat} shows detection power decreasing from 0.38 (SFT) to 0.31 (alignment-RL) to 0.14 (reasoning-RL) at $\delta \geq 0.6$ effect-size threshold, with FPR controlled at $\sim$0.05.
The 63\% drop in reasoning-RL detection power reflects GRPO/PPO training generalizing problem-solving ability rather than memorizing verbatim items, erasing the original-vs-paraphrased performance gap that ConStat relies on.

